On 2 January 2013 08:14, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote:

> On Wed, Jan 2, 2013 at 2:00 PM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com>wrote:
>
>> {lo nu remna cu mleca lo nu vrude kei lo ni ce'u vajni}.
>
>
> I would go with {lo nu remna cu mecvai lo nu vrude}.
>
> It would be one of those "easy lujvo" we discussed long time ago:
>
> {mecyro'e} -> x1=m1 is less than x2=m2 in the aspect/property brode by
> amount x3=m4
>
> {ko'a mecyro'e ko'e ko'i} -> {ko'a mleca ko'e lo ka brode kei ko'i}
>
>
>
You've got it backwards :P It's {rodme'a} -> {mleca fi lo ka broda}. In
your example, the tertau of the veljvo suddenly became the seltau of the
actual meaning; that usually indicates naljvajvo. The trick is that the GDS
(gismu deep structure) is the reverse of the veljvo: {.i mi djica lo nu mi
kansa lo pampe'o lo ka klama lo kindi'u} -> {.i mi kindi'u klama ke pampe'o
kansa ke'e djica} (this one wouldn't be 100% jvajvo, as a lujvo, but it
wouldn't be too far.)

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

